description:
Create src/call_targets/gpu/kernel.rs to own the WGSL compute shader, GPU buffer management, and kernel dispatch for observation aggregation.

## WGSL Shader (embed as a &str constant)
```wgsl
struct Observation { site_idx: u32, sample_base: u32 };
struct Params { sample_count: u32, obs_len: u32, site_start: u32, _pad: u32 };

@group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read>       observations: array<Observation>;
@group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read_write> counts: array<atomic<u32>>;
@group(0) @binding(2) var<storage, read>       params: Params;

@compute @workgroup_size(256)
fn main(@builtin(global_invocation_id) gid: vec3<u32>) {
    let i = gid.x;
    if (i >= params.obs_len) { return; }
    let obs = observations[i];
    let sample_idx = obs.sample_base >> 2u;
    let base_idx   = obs.sample_base & 3u;
    let local_site = obs.site_idx - params.site_start;
    let out_idx    = ((local_site * params.sample_count + sample_idx) * 4u) + base_idx;
    atomicAdd(&counts[out_idx], 1u);
}
```

## GpuAggregateKernel struct
Owns compiled pipeline + persistent buffers sized to max_obs_upload:
```rust
pub(crate) struct GpuAggregateKernel {
    pipeline: wgpu::ComputePipeline,
    bind_group_layout: wgpu::BindGroupLayout,
    obs_buffer: wgpu::Buffer,        // COPY_DST | STORAGE, sized to max_obs_upload * 8 bytes
    params_buffer: wgpu::Buffer,     // COPY_DST | STORAGE, 16 bytes
    pub(crate) max_obs_upload: usize,
}
```

## create_kernel(runtime: &GpuRuntime, max_obs_upload: usize) -> Result<GpuAggregateKernel>
Compile the WGSL shader, create the compute pipeline, create persistent obs and params buffers.

## dispatch(kernel, runtime, counts_buffer, observations, site_start, sample_count) -> Result<()>
For each sub-batch of up to max_obs_upload observations:
1. Write observations to obs_buffer via queue.write_buffer()
2. Write Params { sample_count, obs_len, site_start, _pad: 0 } to params_buffer
3. Create bind group with (obs_buffer, counts_buffer, params_buffer)
4. Encode dispatch_workgroups(ceil(obs_len / 256), 1, 1)
5. Submit command encoder and call device.poll(wgpu::Maintain::Wait)

The counts_buffer is passed in from the chunk — it is allocated by the chunk manager and zeroed at chunk start.

## counts_buffer_size(site_count, sample_count) -> u64
site_count as u64 * sample_count as u64 * 4 * 4 — the count matrix is a flat u32 array, dimensions: sites × samples × 4 bases.
